# #1234 / #1320 (09591683e): the ACCEPTANCE side of the width correction. SPY0348 checks the
# width codegen EMITS, magnitude included — 4294967296 does not fit int, so the literal itself
# emits as long, and arithmetic over it is checked against LONG bounds, not int bounds. Before
# the correction the checker used the un-widened result type and refused these. The refusal
# side (a product that exceeds even long) is pinned by constant_integer_overflow and
# ConstFoldPassTests; this pins the fits-because-it-widened side so a regression that refuses
# valid magnitude-widened constants cannot land silently.
def main() -> None:
    print(4294967296 + 1)
    print(4294967296 * 4)
